  "evaluation": {
    "diagnostics": "Each isolated case materializes Maps/sample.canvas. Start from its document, apply the ordered replacements, and compare the entire Diagnostics object. references names an exact reference_sets array; issues are exact objects. render_check is always not_performed.",
    "replacement": "path is an array of literal object keys or array indices. set replaces or adds, remove removes, append appends. No shell, JSONPath, expression evaluation or product code is used to materialize fixtures.",
    "reference_override": "A case may replace the complete references array. Never append inferred expected records.",
    "hashes": "Compute expected bytes and SHA-256 directly from the authored fixture using UTF-8, ensure_ascii=false, indent=2, and one final LF. Raw cases use their literal UTF-8 bytes, or bytes_hex exclusively.",
    "coverage": "Diagnostic cases compare complete diagnostics; workflow cases assert the listed exact state, reason, changes and file effects. Faults are injected at the named boundary. Missing expected assertions must not be replaced by implementation snapshots.",
    "review": "All-true mechanism-test reviews are synthetic fixtures, not semantic-quality evidence or human approval. The nine meaning examples additionally require a real contextual review.",
    "quality": "For each use, a real review must find the intended information and relations, identify proposals and uncertainties, and reject invented evidence. Schema success alone cannot pass this check."
  },
